      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T14:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Setting up the vsock should be part of starting the VM, shouldn\u0027t it, rather than waiting until we want to send a request? (Suppose we want to send 2 requests to the VM).\n\nAlso, and more importantly: normally we connect from host to VM, to make sure we are connecting to the right VM.\nIn your case I can see why you want to do it this way, because we have no easy way to know when the VM is ready for us to connect to it; but we should still check it\u0027s the right VM. I think you need to find out what the CID of the other end of the socket is, and make sure it matches the CID of the VM you started.",
